# Documentation freshness (Flux)

Before marking Flux work complete:

1. Read [`docs/README-MAINTENANCE-CONTRACT.md`](../../docs/README-MAINTENANCE-CONTRACT.md) when the change touches platform surface area.
2. **Same commit:** meaningful platform changes must update [`README.md`](../../README.md) and/or canonical docs, unless the commit is mechanical with no behavior change (say so in the commit message).
3. **Do not** document aspirational features as shipped. Label **experimental**, **beta**, **internal**, and **operator-only** surfaces honestly.
4. **MCP / tooling** → README MCP section + [`packages/mcp/README.md`](../../packages/mcp/README.md) + [`docs/pages/guides/mcp.md`](../../docs/pages/guides/mcp.md).
5. **CLI / dashboard / gateway / backup / security / deploy** → matching README sections + relevant `docs/pages/*`, `docs/guides/*`, or `docs/OPERATOR-*.md`.
6. **App developer footguns** → [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) + relevant `docs/pages/guides/*`.
7. Run the **documentation checklist** in [`docs/README-MAINTENANCE-CONTRACT.md`](../../docs/README-MAINTENANCE-CONTRACT.md) before finishing.
